WEBVTT

1
00:00:28.583 --> 00:00:30.375
After explaining the importance

2
00:00:30.375 --> 00:00:32.291
of the austerity of speech

3
00:00:32.291 --> 00:00:35.125
in the previous verses of Chapter 17, now

4
00:00:35.125 --> 00:00:37.000
in this verse 17.16

5
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:37.791
Lord Krishna enters

6
00:00:37.791 --> 00:00:40.958
inward – into the field of the mind.

7
00:00:40.958 --> 00:00:42.000
He says –

8
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:46.166
if the body is disciplined and the
speech is restrained,

9
00:00:46.166 --> 00:00:49.375
but the mind remains scattered or impure, then

10
00:00:49.375 --> 00:00:52.916
our progress remains incomplete.

11
00:00:52.916 --> 00:00:56.541
True austerity begins with the mind.

12
00:00:56.541 --> 00:00:59.833
In this verse Lord Krishna describes
manasam tapa –

13
00:00:59.833 --> 00:01:02.791
that is, the austerity of the mind –

14
00:01:02.791 --> 00:01:06.750
and gives a glimpse of what real mental

15
00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:09.416
discipline looks like.

16
00:01:14.291 --> 00:01:16.916
Lord Krishna first tells us –

17
00:01:16.916 --> 00:01:22.250
manah-prasadah – mental contentment.

18
00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:25.333
True contentment does not descend
from the sky,

19
00:01:25.333 --> 00:01:28.291
but is earned through practice.

20
00:01:28.291 --> 00:01:31.125
Circumstances will never be perfect, but

21
00:01:31.125 --> 00:01:32.750
we can choose

22
00:01:32.750 --> 00:01:35.250
to move our vision away from lack

23
00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:36.791
and focus it

24
00:01:36.791 --> 00:01:39.500
on what truly matters.

25
00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:41.708
Contemplating the pastimes of Lord Krishna

26
00:01:41.708 --> 00:01:43.666
and remembering our higher

27
00:01:43.666 --> 00:01:44.833
spiritual goal

28
00:01:44.833 --> 00:01:47.791
develops this contentment.

29
00:01:47.791 --> 00:01:50.708
After this comes saumyata – that is,

30
00:01:50.708 --> 00:01:55.125
gentleness and simplicity of the mind.

31
00:01:55.125 --> 00:01:58.583
Harsh, critical, or overly complicated

32
00:01:58.583 --> 00:02:01.833
thoughts tie knots within us.

33
00:02:01.833 --> 00:02:05.541
Saumyata means keeping the heart soft –

34
00:02:05.541 --> 00:02:06.666
avoiding bitterness

35
00:02:06.666 --> 00:02:10.000
or despair even in difficult circumstances.

36
00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:11.958
It reminds us

37
00:02:11.958 --> 00:02:15.291
that excessive analysis and mental tangles

38
00:02:15.291 --> 00:02:18.958
destroy our peace.

39
00:02:18.958 --> 00:02:22.041
Then comes maunam – silence.

40
00:02:22.041 --> 00:02:24.875
This is not merely staying quiet, but

41
00:02:24.875 --> 00:02:28.416
the depth and dignity of the mind.

42
00:02:28.416 --> 00:02:32.958
This silence stops superficiality and
gives birth to depth

43
00:02:32.958 --> 00:02:36.708
and self-reflection.

44
00:02:36.708 --> 00:02:39.875
After that comes atma-vinigrahah –

45
00:02:39.875 --> 00:02:43.166
that is, self-control.

46
00:02:43.166 --> 00:02:44.125
Every impulse

47
00:02:44.125 --> 00:02:47.625
and every action is born from thought.

48
00:02:47.625 --> 00:02:51.083
Mental austerity means that, instead
of flowing behind every desire

49
00:02:51.083 --> 00:02:54.250
or memory, we return the mind

50
00:02:54.250 --> 00:02:58.083
again and again toward the soul's true shelter –

51
00:02:58.083 --> 00:03:01.000
Lord Krishna.

52
00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:02.083
Finally comes

53
00:03:02.083 --> 00:03:06.000
bhava-shuddhih – purity of feeling.

54
00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:07.625
This is the most subtle of all.

55
00:03:07.625 --> 00:03:09.833
We must continually watch –

56
00:03:09.833 --> 00:03:11.833
is our service

57
00:03:11.833 --> 00:03:14.541
driven by identity and ego,

58
00:03:14.541 --> 00:03:16.708
or by sincerity and truth?

59
00:03:16.708 --> 00:03:18.708
Mental austerity means

60
00:03:18.708 --> 00:03:20.750
purifying our inner motives

61
00:03:20.750 --> 00:03:22.208
again and again,

62
00:03:22.208 --> 00:03:23.958
just as one cleans the temple floor

63
00:03:23.958 --> 00:03:26.000
every day.

64
00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:30.333
When these five qualities –
contentment, gentleness, silence,

65
00:03:30.333 --> 00:03:34.125
restraint, and purity of feeling – come together,

66
00:03:34.125 --> 00:03:35.208
then the mind

67
00:03:35.208 --> 00:03:39.458
becomes not only calm, but pure.

68
00:03:39.458 --> 00:03:43.208
In such a mind spirituality blossoms,
and devotion

69
00:03:43.208 --> 00:03:45.541
flows naturally.

70
00:03:50.291 --> 00:03:53.708
Sometimes we become restless

71
00:03:53.708 --> 00:03:56.500
when others have things

72
00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:59.000
we do not –

73
00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:04.541
better marks, new toys, or more praise.

74
00:04:04.541 --> 00:04:07.833
But instead of repeatedly seeing

75
00:04:07.833 --> 00:04:11.541
what you do not have,

76
00:04:11.541 --> 00:04:14.333
begin to see

77
00:04:14.333 --> 00:04:18.083
what you do have.

78
00:04:18.083 --> 00:04:19.416
Express gratitude for your family,

79
00:04:19.416 --> 00:04:26.250
your home, your food, and your body.

80
00:04:26.250 --> 00:04:30.000
This very feeling is called santosha –
contentment.

81
00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:32.958
When you practise this every day,

82
00:04:32.958 --> 00:04:35.750
your mind becomes calm.

83
00:04:35.750 --> 00:04:39.500
You stop comparing yourself with others.

84
00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:40.208
From within,

85
00:04:40.208 --> 00:04:44.500
you begin to feel lightness and joy.

86
00:04:44.500 --> 00:04:48.000
Envy and comparison are born

87
00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:52.541
when you measure your life by
someone else's scale.

88
00:04:52.541 --> 00:04:54.958
But contentment develops when

89
00:04:54.958 --> 00:04:58.000
you begin to recognise –

90
00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:01.250
what good do I already have!?

91
00:05:01.250 --> 00:05:04.500
And then lift your vision higher –

92
00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:07.083
develop spiritual aspirations,

93
00:05:07.083 --> 00:05:08.916
not material attachments.

94
00:05:08.916 --> 00:05:11.583
When your heart longs for truth, love,

95
00:05:11.583 --> 00:05:15.791
and a deep connection with Me,

96
00:05:15.791 --> 00:05:18.500
then the noise of petty desires

97
00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:21.083
begins to fade on its own.

98
00:05:21.083 --> 00:05:22.916
You do not need to give up

99
00:05:22.916 --> 00:05:24.666
dreaming –

100
00:05:24.666 --> 00:05:26.625
just make sure

101
00:05:26.625 --> 00:05:29.875
that your dreams are deeply
connected to dharma,

102
00:05:29.875 --> 00:05:33.000
and not only to desires.

103
00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:34.000
A contented

104
00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:37.125
mind does not mean giving up ambition –

105
00:05:37.125 --> 00:05:40.708
rather it means that as you grow,

106
00:05:40.708 --> 00:05:44.375
you remain steady and firm from within.

107
00:05:49.083 --> 00:05:50.208
In your family,

108
00:05:50.208 --> 00:05:54.708
silence is not only the absence of noise –

109
00:05:54.708 --> 00:05:57.583
it can also be the experience

110
00:05:57.583 --> 00:06:00.333
of a sacred presence.

111
00:06:00.333 --> 00:06:03.375
Maunam does not mean creating distance

112
00:06:03.375 --> 00:06:05.333
or becoming indifferent.

113
00:06:05.333 --> 00:06:10.333
It means – pausing before speaking,

114
00:06:10.333 --> 00:06:14.166
avoiding gossip,

115
00:06:14.166 --> 00:06:16.791
and not exposing the weaknesses of others

116
00:06:16.791 --> 00:06:21.541
in the name of ordinary conversation.

117
00:06:21.541 --> 00:06:25.500
Relationships do not deepen through
an abundance of words, but

118
00:06:25.500 --> 00:06:27.708
through the respectful

119
00:06:27.708 --> 00:06:31.125
space you give

120
00:06:31.125 --> 00:06:33.375
to others

121
00:06:33.375 --> 00:06:36.666
so that they can express themselves.

122
00:06:36.666 --> 00:06:39.666
When you adopt silence,

123
00:06:39.666 --> 00:06:40.666
you provide

124
00:06:40.666 --> 00:06:42.666
your loved ones a space to breathe

125
00:06:42.666 --> 00:06:45.250
freely, to be seen,

126
00:06:45.250 --> 00:06:49.083
and to feel safe.

127
00:06:49.083 --> 00:06:55.083
If the elders wish to say something
about the traditions of their time,

128
00:06:55.083 --> 00:06:59.875
and they correct you, do not become
irritated with them –

129
00:06:59.875 --> 00:07:02.375
first listen to them with patience,

130
00:07:02.375 --> 00:07:04.625
then explain your point.

131
00:07:04.625 --> 00:07:06.708
A solution will surely be found.

132
00:07:06.708 --> 00:07:11.125
In the same way, the stubbornness of children
should be resolved not by scolding,

133
00:07:11.125 --> 00:07:15.416
 but with sympathy.

134
00:07:15.416 --> 00:07:16.875
Listening more

135
00:07:16.875 --> 00:07:18.541
and speaking less

136
00:07:18.541 --> 00:07:21.625
nourishes the roots of trust.

137
00:07:21.625 --> 00:07:25.666
Commentary is not necessary in every moment.

138
00:07:25.666 --> 00:07:29.916
It is not even necessary to point
out every mistake.

139
00:07:29.916 --> 00:07:34.416
When you are peaceful, people
connect not with your ideas,

140
00:07:34.416 --> 00:07:38.083
but with your presence.

141
00:07:38.083 --> 00:07:43.125
Practise mental depth in the family.

142
00:07:43.125 --> 00:07:48.375
Let your silence not carry a lifeless coldness,

143
00:07:48.375 --> 00:07:50.958
but be filled with affection.

144
00:07:50.958 --> 00:07:55.875
Relationships grow strong through 
that gentle restraint.

145
00:07:55.875 --> 00:08:00.125
And in the stillness between words, true

146
00:08:00.125 --> 00:08:02.125
love begins to speak.

147
00:08:06.750 --> 00:08:09.083
Before managing deadlines, colleagues,

148
00:08:09.083 --> 00:08:11.958
or meetings –

149
00:08:11.958 --> 00:08:14.750
manage your own mind.

150
00:08:14.750 --> 00:08:17.875
Mental austerity itself is the hidden

151
00:08:17.875 --> 00:08:20.083
strength of great leadership.

152
00:08:20.083 --> 00:08:22.875
A calm and contented mind –

153
00:08:22.875 --> 00:08:24.083
manah-prasadah –

154
00:08:24.083 --> 00:08:27.708
does not react with irritation or ego.

155
00:08:27.708 --> 00:08:29.375
A gentle mind –

156
00:08:29.375 --> 00:08:33.250
saumyata – responds with thoughtfulness,

157
00:08:33.250 --> 00:08:35.125
not with criticism.

158
00:08:35.125 --> 00:08:37.583
And maunam does not mean

159
00:08:37.583 --> 00:08:39.583
staying silent in meetings,

160
00:08:39.583 --> 00:08:40.583
but holding within

161
00:08:40.583 --> 00:08:42.208
such a peace

162
00:08:42.208 --> 00:08:45.458
that it brings clarity even in complex situations.

163
00:08:45.458 --> 00:08:47.791
When the mind is scattered,

164
00:08:47.791 --> 00:08:50.666
then even your best strategies

165
00:08:50.666 --> 00:08:53.208
become ineffective.

166
00:08:53.208 --> 00:08:56.250
But when the mind is restrained –

167
00:08:56.250 --> 00:08:59.916
atma-vinigrahah –

168
00:08:59.916 --> 00:09:02.958
then you do not run behind every thought

169
00:09:02.958 --> 00:09:03.583
or feeling

170
00:09:03.583 --> 00:09:07.541
that arises in the mind. And most important is –

171
00:09:07.541 --> 00:09:10.375
watching your own feelings –

172
00:09:10.375 --> 00:09:13.333
bhava-shuddhih.

173
00:09:13.333 --> 00:09:15.875
Are you leading with sincerity,

174
00:09:15.875 --> 00:09:18.083
or only for your own image?

175
00:09:18.083 --> 00:09:22.458
True leadership begins with the mind.

176
00:09:22.458 --> 00:09:27.083
When you discipline your inner world,

177
00:09:27.083 --> 00:09:32.041
then your outer influence grows
on its own, without pressure.
